Fixed: Restrict the single-level overloads of IBTK::LDataManager::spread() and IBTK::LDataManager::interp() to their own level. Before, they crashed if another level contained markers. The overloads that take prolongation or synchronization schedules are deprecated and stop with an error if a schedule for a level finer than the level of the call is not null. Use the overloads without them.
